dreamerv3-torch-genesis — FINAL ROUND ROBIN patch (2026-08-23, genesis_pickaplace/cluster/patches/)
===============================================================================================
Companion to genesis_pickaplace paper/PREREG_final_round_robin_2026-08-23.md (§4.1, §4.3, §5, §9 B4).
Generated against the dev-box copy of dreamerv3-torch-genesis (the cluster tree is newer in
places, e.g. sbatch_genesis_multi.sh carries the 08-18 ARM table there; that file is NOT touched
here -- the new launcher is a separate file so nothing collides).

Apply from the dreamerv3-torch root:
    patch -p1 --dry-run < /path/to/genesis_pickaplace/cluster/patches/dreamerv3-torch-genesis_final_rr.patch
    patch -p1           < /path/to/genesis_pickaplace/cluster/patches/dreamerv3-torch-genesis_final_rr.patch
    chmod +x sbatch_genesis_final_rr.sh
If a hunk fails (cluster file drifted), apply that hunk by hand -- every hunk is small and commented.

What it changes
  1. convert_genesis_demos_repeat.py
       - REFUSES contract-v1 (decision-rate) demo dirs with a pointer to
         genesis_pickaplace/baselines/rl/to_dreamer_native.py (the v1 path: no re-windowing, no relabel).
       - --terminal-guard on|off (DEFAULT on): env-consistent terminals for LEGACY stride-1 tapes via
         full_env.terminal_from_tape (B2): a no-pick tape that tips is cut at the tip decision with
         is_terminal=True; the pick terminal sits at the grant (grant_slack forced 0). `off` reproduces
         the 08-18 sets byte-for-byte. repeat.json gains terminal_guard.
  2. genesis_eval.py
       - --ic-file / --ic-set sel|hold|rnd / --ic-index k: the ONE shared IC file
         (genesis_pickaplace/baselines/eval_ics.json); ints -> demo-uid reset, dicts -> explicit IC.
       - --device (CPU evals with CUDA hidden); per-episode JSON line -> <out>/episodes.jsonl
         (kind, ic_set, ic_index, picked, outcome, n_steps, max_steps, action_repeat, node) for the
         fresh-process sweep; --max-steps help text says the sweep passes 1200 explicitly.
  3. configs.yaml: NEW additive overlay `genesis_final_rr` (time_limit 1200, steps 1e6) stacked after
     genesis_pick_msrecipe [genesis_pick_msrecipe_shaped]; the existing overlays are untouched.
  4. NEW sbatch_genesis_final_rr.sh: one run per job, ARM x REWARD(sparse|dense) x SEED, provenance
     gates (repeat.json stride 4 + contract v1 + demo sha), RUN_REGISTRY check/register at START,
     K=5 checkpoint archive (ckpt_20..100 via a latest.pt watcher on metrics.jsonl step), eval = one
     fresh CPU process per episode on sel (selection) then hold+rnd on the selected (+final) checkpoint,
     asserted denominators, DV3-RESULT line, registry register at END. DRYRUN=1 prints and exits.

Not in this patch (cluster-side, by hand): the genesis_pick_msrecipe_shaped overlay (exists on the
cluster only) -- verify its shaping gamma == discount 0.997 and that it zeroes the potential at the
terminal (PREREG §2) before the dense dv3 arms run.
  (rev 2, after B2's note: the terminal cut lives in the ENCODERS train_sacfd_full.relabel_full /
   delta_encode_transitions_repeat, default on; the converter keeps their done flags and forwards
   --terminal-guard off as terminal_guard=False; it no longer re-derives a terminal itself.)
